Subject: [PATCH] fix(sound): keep block destruction audio single and accurate
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Java event 2014 preserves destruction particles without sound. Use it for Bedrock’s silent destruction event, and when an explicit break sound has already provided audio for the same block. Suppress a later explicit break echo in the reverse packet order. Match the block state and position within a short window so unrelated breaks remain audible.
